HOW THE STORIES MAP TO THE SCHEMA
- Services and their configurable durations, breaks, and capacity -> services (duration_minutes, break_minutes, max_parallel_bookings).
- Bookable schedule / calendar per service -> service_opening_hours (one row per service per day, so Monday-to-Friday and Saturday can differ).
- Breaks and planned off dates (Christmas afternoon, Eid, Diwali, an expert's leave day) -> service_off_periods; service_id NULL means the whole business is closed.
- Booking horizon ("7 days ahead but not the 8th") -> settings (booking_horizon_days).
- Single or multi-person appointments -> appointments + appointment_attendees.
- "Don't allow booking an invalid slot" -> enforced at the application layer: before saving, check (a) the slot is inside service_opening_hours for that weekday, (b) it does not overlap any service_off_period, (c) it is within the configured horizon, (d) the count of overlapping appointments for the service does not exceed max_parallel_bookings, and (e) starts_at/ends_at match the service duration plus break. Optionally add a database-level check in the service: an exclusion-constraint style overlap guard on appointments (starts_at < ends_at) via a CHECK constraint and index on (service_id, starts_at).
